WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.839 --> 00:00:11.718 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Welcome to the Asia capitals, episode seven of seven. First, I clear the
chosen names for a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:12.377 --> 00:00:26.030 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Five capitals of the maritime south-east: the Spanish walled city, the sinking
capital of Java, the sultanate on Borneo, the island city and the far east of
Timor.

3
00:00:26.695 --> 00:00:28.692 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Manila into view.

4
00:00:33.096 --> 00:00:40.259 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Manila stands on the bay in the west of Luzon, in the northern Philippines, on
the South China Sea.

5
00:00:40.918 --> 00:00:50.937 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
From may-nilad, "where the nilad grows", a shrub of its shores. Intramuros,
the walled city the Spanish built, is at its heart.

6
00:00:51.598 --> 00:00:57.821 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Manila as the city where the nilad grows, with the Spanish walled
city at its heart.

7
00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:00.800 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Jakarta into view.

8
00:01:04.722 --> 00:01:11.758 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Jakarta stands on the north coast of Java, in the western part of Indonesia,
facing the Java Sea.

9
00:01:12.423 --> 00:01:25.426 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
From Jayakarta, "complete victory", given in 1527; the Dutch renamed it
Batavia, and the name came back under the Japanese occupation in 1942.

10
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:35.255 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Jakarta as the complete victory that became Batavia and back again,
and the sinking capital that is moving to Borneo.

11
00:01:35.932 --> 00:01:38.695 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Bandar Seri Begawan into view.

12
00:01:41.986 --> 00:01:51.750 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Bandar Seri Begawan stands on the Brunei river in the north-west of Borneo,
facing the water village of Kampong Ayer.

13
00:01:52.414 --> 00:02:01.539 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Named in 1970 in honour of the sultan's father, and the gold-domed Omar Ali
Saifuddien Mosque rises over a lagoon.

14
00:02:02.193 --> 00:02:10.123 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Bandar Seri Begawan as the capital named for a sultan's father, with
the gold mosque over its lagoon.

15
00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:13.015 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Singapore into view.

16
00:02:16.984 --> 00:02:23.973 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Singapore stands on an island at the southern tip of the Malay Peninsula,
facing the Straits.

17
00:02:24.636 --> 00:02:34.957 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
From Sanskrit Singapura, "lion city", though no lions are known to have lived
there. Stamford Raffles founded a British trading post here in 1819.

18
00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:47.220 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Singapore as the lion city where no lions lived, and the trading post
of 1819 that became independent in 1965.

19
00:02:47.986 --> 00:02:50.285 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Dili into view.

20
00:02:59.099 --> 00:03:07.075 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Dili lies on the north coast of Timor, in the east of Timor-Leste, facing the
island of Atauro.

21
00:03:07.733 --> 00:03:20.226 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
It was the capital of Portuguese Timor from 1769, and its statue of Cristo
Rei, 27 m high, stands on a headland east of the town.

22
00:03:20.884 --> 00:03:31.078 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Dili as the Portuguese Timor capital of 1769, with Cristo Rei looking
out over the northern coast.

23
00:03:36.101 --> 00:03:52.181 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Manila is in the north of the Philippines, Jakarta on the north coast of Java,
Bandar Seri Begawan across Borneo's river, Singapore at the tip of the
peninsula, and Dili on the north coast of Timor.

24
00:03:52.836 --> 00:04:04.516 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember where the nilad grows, the complete victory that became Batavia, the
gold mosque over its lagoon, the lion city where no lions lived, and Cristo
Rei above the northern coast.
